# Agent Session Pack — process environment notes
#
# The CLI reads process.env at runtime. It does not load dotenv (or any
# .env file) by itself. Export variables in your shell, or use tooling such
# as direnv that injects into the process environment before the CLI starts.
# Do not commit a real .env with machine-specific or secret values.

# HOME — required
# Used to resolve vault and config paths (default: ~/.agent-session-pack)
# and provider session store roots under your home directory.
# Usually set by the login shell on macOS/Linux.
# Example:
# HOME=/Users/you
